<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11375" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrythus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κόρυθος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An ancient town in Etruria</i>, so named from its
			mythical founder, later called <i>Cortona</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				209</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 719</span></i>.—<b>Poet.</b>, in gen., for <i>Etruria</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 9,
				10</span></i>; and for <i>Italia</i>,
					<i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 170</span></i> Forbig. ad
			loc.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A companion of Perseus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5,
				125</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Son of Paris and Œnone</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				361</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>One of the Lapithæ</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				290</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
